iple purposes: it extracts value from weaker hands, denies free equity to drawing hands (straight and flush draws are possible), and keeps the pot small in case I'm behind. Given the opponent's passive play, they're unlikely to have a strong hand like top pair Queens or better. Checking would be too weak and gives free cards to draws.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
